Introduction
============

ChmSee is an HTML Help viewer for Unix/Linux. It is based on CHMLIB
and use GTK+ as its frontend toolkit. Because of using webkit HTML
rendering engine, ChmSee can support rich features of modern HTML
page, specially CSS.

Homepage: https://github.com/h1aji/chmsee


Dependencies
============

To compile ChmSee from source, the following packages should have been
installed and met their version on your system:

 * cmake >= 3.16
 * pkg-config
 * GTK 3.24 (gtk+-3.0)
 * WebKit2GTK 4.1 (webkit2gtk-4.1, the GTK 3 / libsoup 3 API)
 * chmlib >= 0.39
 * libxml2
 * gettext (msgfmt, for translations)

Installation
============

$ cmake -S . -B build
$ cmake --build build
# cmake --install build

Debian package
==============

On Debian/Ubuntu, install the build dependencies above plus dpkg-dev and
file (used to detect shared-library dependencies), then:

$ cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr
$ cmake --build build
$ cpack --config build/CPackConfig.cmake -G DEB -B dist

The GitHub Actions "Build Debian package" workflow builds the same package
on Ubuntu 24.04 and uploads the .deb as the `chmsee-deb` workflow artifact.
The package's shared-library dependencies are generated by dpkg-shlibdeps.

Source code repository
======================

You can use git command below to retrive develping ChmSee code:

$ git clone https://github.com/h1aji/chmsee.git

Report bug
==========

If you encounter any ChmSee problem, please report them to
https://github.com/h1aji/chmsee

